  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0301, and it contains four tables. The first table, Seat_Template, has three columns: description, template_ID, and template_name. The template_ID column is the primary key, and the description and template_name columns are both strings. The second table, User, has four columns: contact_number, email, name, and user_ID. The user_ID column is the primary key, and the other columns are all strings. The third table, Seat, has ten columns: column, creation_time, flag, location_X, location_Y, price, reservedPurchasedUserID, row, seat_ID, type, and update_time. The seat_ID column is the primary key, and the other columns are all integers or strings. The fourth table, Seat_Template_Layout, has four columns: occasion, seat_ID, template_ID, and time_period. The seat_ID and template_ID columns are both foreign keys that reference the Seat and Seat_Template tables, respectively. The occasion column is a string, and the time_period column is also a string. The primary key for this table is a composite key made up of the seat_ID and template_ID columns.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\nThis database can be used for an online seat reservation system, such as for cinemas, theaters, or conference halls. The system can record and manage seat information for different areas, including seat locations (X-coordinate, Y-coordinate, row, column), type, price, creation time, update time, etc. The system can mark the validity of seats using a flag field, such as whether a seat has been reserved or purchased. The system supports multiple seat layout templates, including template name and description, which are suitable for different occasions or time periods. Users have a unique ID, name, contact number, and email address. Users can query available seats based on seat location, type, price, etc. Users can select seats online for reservation or purchase, and the system will update the seat status accordingly.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0301.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0301\nCREATE TABLE `seat_template` (\n  `template_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `template_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`template_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `seat` (\n  `seat_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `row` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `column` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location_x` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location_y` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `flag` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reserved_purchased_user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`seat_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `seat_template_layout` (\n  `seat_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `template_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `occasion` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `time_period` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`seat_id`, `template_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `seat_template_layout_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`seat_id`) REFERENCES `seat` (`seat_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `seat_template_layout_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`template_id`) REFERENCES `seat_template` (`template_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
